.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "April 2026" "1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"

.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command line interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a minimal UNIX command line interpreter (shell).
It reads commands from standard input, one per line,
and executes them using
.BR execve (2).

In interactive mode, a prompt is displayed before each command.
In non-interactive mode, commands are read from a pipe or file.

.SH USAGE
Interactive mode:
.RS
.nf
$ ./hsh
($) /bin/ls
($) exit
.fi
.RE

Non-interactive mode:
.RS
.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the shell is the exit status of the last command executed.
If a command is not found, the exit status is 127.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The current environment is passed to executed commands via
.BR execve (2).

